# Safe QLD
/android
/ios
*.apk
*.aab
.env

# Customer panel configurations. These are live site data — Grange Hall,
# Ipswich Hospital and the rest are real buildings — and they are used for
# parser development only, never committed. Tests that read them skip when
# they are absent.
*.ffp
*.nle
*.pci
*.pcf
*.sts
*.ncf
*.NCF
*.accdb
*.mdb
*.util

# Customer asset registers and reports. The register export is Safe QLD's live
# book of work — 12,553 assets across 897 named sites, with addresses and
# locations — and the report examples are real jobs for real buildings. Used
# for development only, never committed. Tests that read them skip when absent.
*.csv
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.docx
!data/*.template.csv
/data/registers/

# Compiled output next to a TypeScript source shadows it: jest and Metro both
# resolve the .js first, so the app and the suite quietly read a stale copy of
# a file somebody is actively editing. This happened once with the standards
# catalogue and cost an afternoon of edits that appeared to do nothing.
src/**/*.js
src/**/*.js.map
src/**/*.d.ts
app/**/*.js
app/**/*.js.map

# Editor and script backups. Not a resolution hazard the way a compiled .js is,
# but 55KB of stale duplicate turns up in every grep and reads as live code to
# whoever finds it next.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
# The directory and, in a worktree, the symlink to it.
node_modules
node_modules/
